    {
      "id": "QamNidqqtyXgdG78yoas0",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 201.49342234981467,
      "y": 1437.7531149193958,
      "width": 526.5300574714202,
      "height": 1000,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "aC",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 2123355569,
      "version": 1636,
      "versionNonce": 1220963533,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1779628787079,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "freqs = {x:2, y:1, z:1}\nbank =  {x:2, y:1, z:1}\nl=0->a:\n    r=0->a:\nso thered be a if(*r in freqs), bank[*r]--\n        a not in freqs->nothing\n        bank not empty->advance r\n    r=1\n        bank[x]-- -> bank = {x1,y1,z1}\n        bank not empty\n    r=2: nothing\n    r=3:\n        bank = {x1,y0,z1}\nthen thered be another if saying \"if bank[*r]==0,\nremove\"\n        bank = {x1,z1}\n    ... till r=5\n        bank empty->update min (5-0+1=6)\n        while (*l not in freqs):\n            l++\n        bank.insert({*l, 1})\n\nnow this could be a new min, so actually i think its\nbest to move the min update here\nsince for normal r expansion, *l is in anyway so the\nwhile is skipped\nanyway now we're at l=1 r=5 bank={x:1} min=5\n\nl=1\n    r=6\n        a not in -> bank still {x:1}\n        now we've reached end and bank not empty-\n>end with min 5\n\nisnt that it? seems simple for a hard...\nlets implement\n        \n        \n        \n        ",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "freqs = {x:2, y:1, z:1}\nbank =  {x:2, y:1, z:1}\nl=0->a:\n    r=0->a:\nso thered be a if(*r in freqs), bank[*r]--\n        a not in freqs->nothing\n        bank not empty->advance r\n    r=1\n        bank[x]-- -> bank = {x1,y1,z1}\n        bank not empty\n    r=2: nothing\n    r=3:\n        bank = {x1,y0,z1}\nthen thered be another if saying \"if bank[*r]==0, remove\"\n        bank = {x1,z1}\n    ... till r=5\n        bank empty->update min (5-0+1=6)\n        while (*l not in freqs):\n            l++\n        bank.insert({*l, 1})\n\nnow this could be a new min, so actually i think its best to move the min update here\nsince for normal r expansion, *l is in anyway so the while is skipped\nanyway now we're at l=1 r=5 bank={x:1} min=5\n\nl=1\n    r=6\n        a not in -> bank still {x:1}\n        now we've reached end and bank not empty->end with min 5\n\nisnt that it? seems simple for a hard...\nlets implement\n        \n        \n        \n        ",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
